@startuml Authentication
title Authentication: Register with OTP, Login, Token Refresh and Password Reset
autonumber

actor User
boundary "Auth Modal" as UI
participant "HTTP Client\n(Axios interceptors)" as Http
control "Auth Controller" as Controller
control "Auth Handlers (CQRS)" as Handlers
participant "Email Service\n(Nodemailer SMTP)" as Mail
database "Redis" as Redis
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Register (two-step OTP verification) ==
User -> UI: Fill Sign Up form (name, email, password, role)
UI -> UI: Check password strength and confirmation match
UI -> Http: POST /api/v1/auth/send-register-otp { email }
Http -> Controller: Forward request
Controller -> Handlers: SendRegisterOtpCommand(email)
Handlers -> DB: Find user by email
alt Email already registered
    Handlers --> Controller: 409 Conflict
    Controller --> UI: Email already exists
    UI --> User: Suggest signing in instead
else Email available
    Handlers -> Handlers: Generate 6-digit OTP
    Handlers -> Redis: SET otp:register:{email} EX 300
    Handlers -> Mail: Send verification email
    Mail --> User: OTP delivered to inbox
    Handlers --> Controller: OTP sent
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK
    UI --> User: Show OTP input with countdown
end

User -> UI: Enter 6-digit OTP
UI -> Http: POST /api/v1/auth/verify-otp { email, otp, type: register }
Http -> Controller: Forward request
Controller -> Handlers: VerifyOtpCommand
Handlers -> Redis: GET otp:register:{email}
alt OTP wrong or expired
    Handlers --> Controller: 400 Bad Request
    Controller --> UI: Invalid or expired OTP
    UI --> User: Show error and Resend OTP option
else OTP matches
    Handlers -> Redis: DEL otp:register:{email}
    Handlers -> Redis: SET otp:verified:register:{email} EX 900
    Handlers --> Controller: Verified
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK
    UI -> Http: POST /api/v1/auth/register { name, email, password, role }
    Http -> Controller: Forward request
    Controller -> Handlers: RegisterCommand
    Handlers -> Redis: Check otp:verified:register:{email}
    Handlers -> Handlers: Hash password with bcrypt (10 rounds)
    Handlers -> DB: Insert user with role
    Handlers -> Handlers: Sign accessToken (15m) and refreshToken (7d)
    Handlers -> Redis: SET refresh_token:{userId} EX 7d
    Handlers --> Controller: User + token pair
    Controller --> UI: 201 Created
    UI -> UI: Save user and tokens in auth.store
    UI --> User: Show avatar, name and role in navbar
end

== Login ==
User -> UI: Enter email and password
UI -> Http: POST /api/v1/auth/login
Http -> Controller: Forward request
Controller -> Handlers: LoginCommand
Handlers -> DB: Find user by email
alt User missing or bcrypt compare fails
    Handlers --> Controller: 401 Unauthorized
    Controller --> UI: Invalid credentials
    UI --> User: Show error
else Credentials valid
    Handlers -> Handlers: Sign accessToken (sub, email, role)
    Handlers -> Redis: SET refresh_token:{userId} EX 7d
    Handlers --> Controller: User + token pair
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK
    UI -> UI: Persist session in auth.store
    UI --> User: Signed in
end

== Authenticated request and silent token refresh ==
UI -> Http: Any API call (e.g. GET /api/v1/auth/me)
Http -> Http: Inject Authorization: Bearer {accessToken}
Http -> Controller: Request with JWT
alt Access token valid
    Controller --> Http: 200 OK + data
    Http --> UI: Response
else Access token expired
    Controller --> Http: 401 Unauthorized
    Http -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh { refreshToken }
    Controller -> Handlers: RefreshTokenCommand
    Handlers -> Redis: Compare with refresh_token:{userId}
    Handlers -> DB: Check user is still active
    alt Refresh token valid
        Handlers -> Redis: Store rotated refresh token
        Handlers --> Controller: New token pair
        Controller --> Http: 200 OK
        Http -> Http: Update auth.store
        Http -> Controller: Replay original request with new token
        Controller --> Http: 200 OK + data
        Http --> UI: Response
    else Refresh token invalid or expired
        Controller --> Http: 401 Unauthorized
        Http -> UI: logout()
        UI --> User: Session ended, show Sign In
    end
end

== Forgot and reset password ==
User -> UI: Open Forgot Password, enter email
UI -> Http: POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password { email }
Http -> Controller: Forward request
Controller -> Handlers: ForgotPasswordCommand
Handlers -> DB: Find user by email
alt User not found
    Handlers --> Controller: 404 Not Found
    Controller --> UI: Email not registered
else User exists
    Handlers -> Redis: SET otp:reset:{email} EX 300
    Handlers -> Mail: Send password reset OTP
    Mail --> User: Reset OTP delivered
    Handlers --> Controller: OTP sent
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK
end

User -> UI: Enter OTP, new password and confirmation
UI -> Http: POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password { email, otp, newPassword }
Http -> Controller: Forward request
Controller -> Handlers: ResetPasswordCommand
Handlers -> Redis: GET otp:reset:{email}
alt OTP wrong or expired
    Handlers --> Controller: 400 Bad Request
    Controller --> UI: Invalid or expired OTP
else OTP matches
    Handlers -> Handlers: Hash new password with bcrypt
    Handlers -> DB: Update user password hash
    Handlers -> Redis: DEL otp:reset:{email}
    Handlers --> Controller: Password updated
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK
    UI --> User: Ask to sign in with the new password
end

@enduml
